  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to Hardy&#39;s -schulz rule, greater the valency of the active ion or flocculating ion greater will be its coagulating power. <math><msup><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi></math> charged colloid so cation having more <math><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi></math> charge, more will be coagulating power.<br /><br />Hence <math><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> having maximum coagulating power",
